$first_image — keep only the first input image

SUMMARY
  Reduces the images[] array to a single element: the first link from the
  incoming bundle. All other arrays are passed through unchanged.

SYNTAX
  $first_image

INPUT
  images[] — one or more image links (required for non-empty output)

OUTPUT
  images[] — [images[0]] if the input had at least one image, else []

ARGUMENTS
  None.

BEHAVIOR
  Does not copy or re-encode image files; the same session link is kept.
  Useful after $image(...)[n] or parallel branches when downstream steps
  should process only one frame.

EXAMPLE
  @hero: @gallery -> $first_image -> $image2image

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
